yamlvalidate — validate YAML files against a JSON Schema

Usage:
  yamlvalidate [flags]
  yamlvalidate [command]

Available Commands:
  completion  Generate the autocompletion script for the specified shell
  help        Help about any command
  validate    Validate YAML files against a JSON Schema

Flags:
      --config string       path to a config file
      --debug               raise log verbosity to debug (alias for --log-level debug)
  -h, --help                help for yamlvalidate
      --log-format string   log format: auto, text, or json (default "auto")
      --log-level string    log verbosity: error, warn, info, or debug (default "warn")
      --no-color            disable colored output
      --no-input            never prompt; run non-interactively
  -o, --output string       output format: text or json (default "text")
  -q, --quiet               suppress progress and non-error logs
  -v, --verbose             raise log verbosity to info (alias for --log-level info)
      --version             version for yamlvalidate

Use "yamlvalidate [command] --help" for more information about a command.
